  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing the \"Dashboard\" screen for VermurOps. The core is the header: \"Dashboard,\" accompanied by a subtitle greeting the user and displaying the current date. I\'m aiming for simplicity in the date format, ensuring clarity for the user.\n\n\n**Defining Key Performance Indicators**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the Key Performance Indicators (KPIs). I envision four cards on a white background with muted labels and sparklines. \"Embarques activos,\" \"Cotizaciones pendientes,\" \"Clientes activos,\" and \"Ingresos del mes\" are the initial KPIs. Delta values with arrows will show changes compared to the previous week, using green for positive changes and muted neutrals. I am aiming for concise and clear presentations.\n\n\n**Structuring the Dashboard Layout**\n\nI\'m now diving into the structural layout. I\'m visualizing a main content area taking up two-thirds of the space, with a side panel occupying the remaining third. The KPIs will sit at the top, presented as a grid across the screen. Underneath this, the main content area will hold the alert and table, and the side panel will display the \"Tareas pendientes\" and \"Pr\303\263ximos vencimientos\". I\'m aiming for a responsive grid to accommodate different screen sizes. My goal is to use `lg:grid-cols-3` with the main content spanning two columns.\n\n\n**Refining the Header Strategy**\n\nI\'m now wrestling with the header implementation. Should I handle the \"Dashboard\" title and subtitle within `App.tsx`, or delegate it entirely to `Dashboard.tsx`? The top bar is already present in `App.tsx`, so it might be better to keep the title there, and handle the greeting as a hero header in `Dashboard.tsx`, similar to Linear. The key consideration is the existing sticky top bar in `App.tsx`. I think I will let `App.tsx` handle the title, and the greeting can be handled as the hero header in `Dashboard.tsx`, as the subtitle with date should be handled on the dashboard level.\n\n\n**Revising Header Implementation**\n\nI\'m now revising the header implementation. I am considering putting \"Dashboard\" in `App.tsx` and adding the greeting with the date in `Dashboard.tsx`, at the top. I think I will add this to the `Dashboard.tsx` canvas with a title and subtitle.\nI\'ve already started sketching the structure and found that `App.tsx` already has a dashboard title, but this is a bit too much, and I will be changing it. I\'m aiming for simplicity.\n\n\n**Implementing Static Data**\n\nI\'m now implementing the static data requested for the recent shipments table. I\'ve defined an array of shipment objects, including details like ID, client, origin, destination, mode, status, and ETA. I\'ve also added a list for pending tasks, including titles and done status. I\'m focusing on ensuring data integrity.\n\n\n**Mapping Status & KPIs**\n\nI\'m now mapping status strings to color-coded badges, ensuring visual consistency. I\'ve also defined specific KPI values and deltas, including \"Embarques activos,\" \"Cotizaciones pendientes,\" \"Clientes activos,\" and \"Ingresos\" with their corresponding delta changes. I\'m focusing on color-coding for status and using appropriate deltas for KPIs. I\'m also refining the background style for the KPI cards.\n\n\n**Refining KPI Card Styles**\n\nI\'m now refining the style for the KPI cards. I am using a base structure for each card, with a subtle background and border, and am working on improving visual hierarchy. I am focusing on the balance between the KPIs values and labels, along with sparklines, deltas, and colors. I am aiming for clarity.\n\nI\'m focusing on the component for the KPI cards, and I am incorporating a sparkline. I\'ve designed the card to accommodate the KPI with a title, value, and delta. I\'ve defined a layout to accommodate the elements. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and clarity.\nI\'ve already added a header: \"Embarques activos,\" and a value: \"3\" with the delta: \"+1 vs. semana pasada.\" I\'m also adding a color code. I\'ve started the structure for the alert band.\n\n\n**Implementing the Alert Component**\n\nI\'m now starting on the alert band, focusing on its visual hierarchy. I\'ve begun with the structure of the alert band and added some placeholder content. The main container is below KPIs and consists of a grid with 3 columns on larger screens; the left takes two, and the right takes one. My goal is to add the table, tasks, and vencimientos components in the next step.\n\nI\'m also considering adjusting the `App.tsx` header to keep it clean, simply showing \"Dashboard.\" In the `Dashboard.tsx` component, I\'ll add a header for the screen itself.\nI am also planning on adding a subtitle to the header.\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mb-[32px]\">\n  <h2 className=\"text-[20px] font-semibold text-text-primary tracking-tight\">Dashboard</h2>\n  <p className=\"text-[14px] text-text-secondary\">Subtitle Text</p>\n</div>\n```\n\n\n**Updating Header Component**\n\nI\'m now revising the header implementation, aiming for cleaner code. I\'m removing the title from `App.tsx` when on the dashboard to allow `Dashboard.tsx` to handle its own title. I\'ll add the necessary logic to refine it in both components. I\'m also planning on implementing a sparkline SVG for the KPI cards, considering alternative designs for the lines.\nI\'m also considering the dashboard title.\nI am also thinking of removing the dashboard title from `App.tsx` and handling it in `Dashboard.tsx`.\n\n\n**Refactoring Dashboard Structure**\n\nI\'m currently undertaking a `Dashboard.tsx` rewrite for greater modularity. The goal is to keep `App.tsx` streamlined, shifting dashboard-specific components to `Dashboard.tsx`. I am aiming for a clean separation of concerns. I am adding a new structure with a header and a subtitle in the dashboard component. I am incorporating sparklines within the KPI cards, and implementing `SparklineUp` and `SparklineFlat` components.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Display**\n\nI\'ve added static data for recent shipments with IDs, clients, and statuses. Upcoming deadlines include titles and dates. The focus is data rendering. I\'m aiming to add a color-coding function for visual statuses.\n\n```\n*   Implement a color-coding function for shipment statuses, ensuring visual consistency across the dashboard.\n*   Added the getStatusColor function.\n*   Added an array of shipment objects.\n*   Added an array of upcoming deadlines.\n```\n\n\n**Adding Data & Alerts**\n\nI\'m now integrating shipment statuses with visual color-coding for data clarity. I\'m adding an array of shipments and deadlines. I\'m also adding a function to determine the color-coded badge. I\'m implementing a task-toggle functionality.\n\nI\'m working on the data display. I\'ve added a function to retrieve the color of the status, according to what it is. I\'ve also implemented an array with tasks, and a toggle function.\n\n\n**Implementing KPI Cards**\n\nI\'m now implementing the structure for the individual KPI cards, focusing on a clear presentation for each metric. I\'ve already structured each with title, sparkline, value, and delta. I\'m aiming for responsive layouts and clear visual hierarchy within each card, with a goal for the design to match the other components in the dashboard. I\'ve designed a layout that accommodates each element.\n\n\n**Implementing KPI Cards**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the KPI cards. I am working on structuring each card to clearly display title, sparkline, value, and delta. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and visual consistency. I\'ve designed the card to accommodate the title and value, delta and sparkline. I\'m aiming for designs that match the dashboard.\n\n\n**Finalizing KPI Implementation**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the KPI cards, focusing on their integration and visual polish. I\'ve structured a KPI card to have a background color, padding, rounded corners and a border. I am incorporating a sparkline SVG at the top of the card. I\'ve designed the card for responsiveness and visual clarity, including a sparkline, title, value and delta. My aim is to match the other components of the dashboard.\n\n\n**Adding Alert Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating an alert band with an operational alert and a \"Revisar\" button. The alert includes a brief message about shipments needing documentation. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, visual hierarchy, and ensuring it integrates well with the dashboard\'s design. The alert band uses an icon, a descriptive message, and a button.\n\n```html\n          <div className=\"bg-card border-l-[3px] border-l-brand border-y border-r border-y-card-border border-r-card-border py-[16px] px-[20px] rounded-r-[12px] rounded-l-[4px] flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between shadow-sm\">\n            <div className=\"flex items-center text-[14px]\">\n              <AlertCircle className=\"w-[18px] h-[18px] text-brand mr-[12px]\" />\n              <strong className=\"text-text-primary mr-[6px] font-medium\">Alerta operativa:</strong>\n              <span className=\"text-text-secondary\">2 embarques requieren documentaci\303\263n.</span>\n            </div>\n            <button className=\"mt-3 sm:mt-0 bg-white border border-card-border text-text-primary px-[16px] py-[8px] rounded-[8px] text-[13px] font-medium hover:bg-neutral-bg transition-colors shadow-sm whitespace-nowrap\">\n              Revisar\n            </button>\n          </div>\n```\n\n\n**Structuring the Shipments Table**\n\nI\'m now structuring the recent shipments table, aiming for a clear display of data. I\'m adding headers for shipment ID, client, origin/destination, mode, status, and ETA. The table uses `thead` with labels that are small, uppercase, and muted. Each row is styled with padding and borders. I\'m focusing on ensuring data is organized and easy to read.\n\n\n\n**Structuring the Shipments Table**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the recent shipments table. I\'m focusing on the table\'s header and ensuring that headers for the table are clear, small, and uppercase. I\'m using `thead` and `tbody` and aiming for organized data in each row, with padding and borders.\n\n\n**Implementing Table Content**\n\nI\'m now implementing the content for the shipments table, including displaying shipment details like origin, destination, mode, status, and ETA. I am incorporating a color-coding function for the status badges. I\'m focusing on ensuring data is correctly rendered within the table structure. I\'m aiming for clarity in displaying each shipment\'s information.\n\n\n**Implementing Task Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating the pending tasks list into the dashboard. I\'ve designed a list with checkable items. Each item includes a check button and a task description. The list renders from the task array I defined previously. I\'m focusing on making the list interactive and clear, using colors for the tasks and making the tasks strikethrough after checking them. I\'m also ensuring the tasks are clickable.\n\nI\'m now working on making the tasks clickable, and toggleable. I\'ve also implemented the strikethrough.\n\nI\'ve also just implemented the display for the component.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the dashboard, completing the integration of all components. I am confirming proper alignment and responsiveness across the entire layout. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual consistency and overall user experience. I am aiming to ensure that all data is rendered correctly and the interaction is seamless.\n\n\n**Refining Dashboard Completion**\n\nI\'m now refining the dashboard\'s completion. The `SparklineUp` fix is done, and the checkboxes are sleek. I\'ve updated `Dashboard.tsx` with these improvements. I\'m also revising the top bar in `App.tsx`; the title will be just \"Dashboard\", like standard dashboards, or maybe remove the text? I\'m assessing the options for the title.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
