  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Quote Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the \"Quotes\" section, specifically implementing the header with \"New Quote\" button. I\'m considering subtle filters for status, client, mode, and date ranges. Also, I\'m working on the structure for the table.\n\n\n**Defining Quote Details**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the structure of the quote table, envisioning columns for Quote ID, Client, Route (Mode + Origin \342\206\222 Destination), Date, Validity, Value, and Status. I\'m also planning a row-action menu for viewing, editing, duplicating, converting, and PDF downloading. I\'m visualizing the \"New Quote\" flow, including fields for client, mode, incoterm, origin, and destination, along with editable line items for charges, and auto-calculated margins. I\'m thinking of save draft and send to client buttons.\n\n**Outlining Rate Management**\n\nI\'ve initiated the rate management module. My goal is to organize rates by route, mode, and carrier in a structured table. I am envisioning a rate control center.\n\n\n**Refining Rate Structure**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the rate structure, considering factors like validity, surcharges, and the distinction between spot and contract rates, along with target margins. I am developing filters for origin, destination, mode, and carrier to enhance rate management. I\'m planning to include a \"Nueva tarifa\" and \"Importar tarifario\" button, and have plans to implement a search bar, reminiscent of a \"control tower\", to compare rates across different carriers for a given route. I have started updating `data.ts` to include or mock requested quotes. I may instead locally define them in `Quotes.tsx`. I am also planning the new `RatesManagement.tsx` component.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 258985060
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
