    thinking: "**Designing Customs Module**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing the new customs compliance module for Mexico, specifically considering the screen requirements. The header will be \"Aduanas\" with a \"Nuevo despacho\" primary button. I\'m also planning to include KPIs like \"Pendientes de despacho,\" \"En revisi\303\263n,\" \"Liberados hoy,\" and \"Pedimentos por pagar\" for quick access to key information.\n\n\n**Building Customs Table**\n\nI\'ve been working on the table of customs clearances. It will include columns for Pedimento number, Shipment, Client, Customs broker, Customs office, Type, Tariff code, Status, and Date. I\'m also including statuses like \"En clasificaci\303\263n,\" \"Documentando,\" \"En revisi\303\263n,\" \"Liberado,\" and \"Rojo aduanero,\" each with a corresponding color. I linked mock data to \"SHP-2023-003\" which is \"En aduana.\" The detail view will feature Pedimento data, customs broker details, tariff information, tax calculations, a document checklist, and a timeline.\n\nI am planning to implement the code in `/src/components/Customs.tsx` and adding it to `/src/App.tsx` and `/src/components/Sidebar.tsx` using the `Scale` icon from lucide-react. I will then work on building the UI.\n\n\n"
