  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing BI Dashboard**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting a Reports & BI dashboard, and the user\'s feedback clarifies replacing the placeholder. The user specifically requests replacing the \'Reports\' placeholder with a full-fledged analytical dashboard. The \"Reemplaza el placeholder \'M\303\263dulo de BI\" is an important note, pointing to something that the dashboard will need to do, it seems.\n\n\n**Constructing Reports Component**\n\nI realize the \'Reports\' placeholder in `App.tsx` requires an actual `Reports` component. I\'m now tasked with building `/src/components/Reports.tsx`. It needs a top section with date range selection, filters (client, mode, route), and an \"Export\" button. Then, it needs KPI cards for revenue, margin, shipments, quote conversion, and clearance time. Finally, I\'ll need to create placeholder charts: a line graph for monthly revenue, and bar graphs for shipments by mode.\n\n\n**Designing Report Interface**\n\nNow I\'m designing the layout of the `Reports.tsx` component. I\'m structuring the component with a sidebar for saved reports and a main area for KPIs and the dashboard itself. I\'m leaning toward a grid layout, probably with a 4-column structure, using Tailwind classes. The top bar will hold date range selection, filters, and an \"Export\" option. I\'ll need to create donut charts for quotes by status, a table for top clients by revenue and margin, and a funnel chart to visualize the quote lifecycle, from the quote to invoice.\n\n\n**Analyzing Report Component Layout**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the UI structure for the report component and focusing on the overall layout. My latest thought is the placement of the saved reports panel. I\'m considering either a left sidebar, a right sidebar, or a layout where the panel is under the top bar. I\'m starting to lean towards placing the side panel on the right. I\'m also planning the grid structure for the KPI cards and the dashboard charts.\n\n\n**Implementing Chart Placeholders**\n\nI\'m now implementing placeholder HTML/CSS for the charts. I\'ve created an SVG for the line chart, using a polyline for visual representation. For the bar charts, I am using a flexbox with items aligned to the bottom, and basic color-coded divs to represent the bars. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, and I\'m using `w-full` and `h-full` to ensure the chart place holders fill their container.\n\n\n**Refining Chart Placeholders**\n\nI\'ve switched from trying to calculate `strokeDasharray` in SVG for the donut charts, and I have found that CSS `conic-gradient` is a much simpler approach for them. I\'m now implementing stacked divs for a funnel chart, which seems simpler than the alternatives.\n\n\n**Structuring Reports Component**\n\nI\'m now structuring the `Reports.tsx` file and defining the layout, and I\'ve started the implementation of the funnel chart with stacked divs, following an updated approach. I\'ve also identified basic placeholder cards.\n\n\n**Defining KPI Data**\n\nI\'m now defining the structure for the key performance indicator (KPI) data. I\'ve got the initial data points: Revenue, Average Margin, Shipments by Mode, Quote Conversion, and Average Customs Time. I\'m noting the actual values and the percent changes. I\'m going to start populating this information to the placeholder cards.\n\n\n\n**Refining Component Interface**\n\nI\'m now integrating the date range, filter, and export components into the report interface, using the provided styles. I\'m focusing on ensuring these elements are visually consistent with the existing design elements.\n\n\n**Integrating Export Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the export functionality within the Reports component, following the UI structure and styling guidelines. I\'m focusing on ensuring the \"Export\" button is positioned correctly and visually consistent. I\'m also preparing for the implementation of the download functionality.\n\n\n**Populating KPI Cards**\n\nI\'m now populating the KPI cards with data, and I\'ve started on cards 2 and 3. I\'m focusing on layout, and adding the relevant data (actual values and percentage changes) to the placeholder components. I am using Tailwind for styling.\n\n\n**Populating KPI Cards**\n\nI\'m now populating the KPI cards. I am working on the remaining cards, focusing on aligning the data with the design. I\'m ensuring consistency with the styling for all KPI components, including the new design.\n\n\n**Finalizing KPI Cards**\n\nI\'m now completing the KPI cards, focusing on the Average Customs Time. I\'m adding the relevant data and ensuring visual consistency with the other cards and their corresponding elements. The data display and format are currently being reviewed to check for accuracy.\n\n\n**Implementing Line Chart**\n\nI\'m now implementing the monthly revenue line chart. I\'ve noted the latest design details for the line chart, and I\'ve started integrating the placeholder. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, and I\'m ensuring the chart fills its container, as well as considering the structure of the data display. I\'m focusing on the trend representation using the latest data from the design.\n\n\n**Constructing Line Chart**\n\nI\'m now implementing the line chart, and incorporating the polyline with responsive dimensions. I\'m focusing on the data points. I\'m building on the existing placeholders for the monthly data, and ensuring the data labels and the chart align correctly. I\'m also now adding the responsive attributes and the color schema to this chart.\n\n\n**Developing Bar Charts**\n\nI\'m now developing the shipment mode bar charts, focusing on dynamic data rendering. I\'m adding hover effects to show values and labels, and I\'m ensuring visual consistency with the design for the existing chart. I\'ve updated the responsive attributes. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and visual integration, and I am also adding the transitions and colors.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the bar chart\'s visual elements, like hover effects, and transitions, ensuring consistency with the overall report design. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and ensuring the chart data is displayed properly. I\'ve also incorporated the correct color schema. I\'ve started on integrating the donut charts.\n\n\n**Implementing Donut Charts**\n\nI\'m now implementing the donut charts for quote status, using CSS conic gradients for a smoother approach. I am now focusing on refining the visual representation of the percentage data, for accepted, sent, and expired/rejected quotes. I\'m focusing on ensuring responsiveness.\n\n\n**Developing Donut Representation**\n\nI\'m now completing the implementation of the donut chart for the quote statuses, using conic gradients. I\'m focusing on responsiveness. I\'m focusing on ensuring accurate representation of the percentage data in the chart, and updating the labels and their representation.\n\n\n\n**Constructing Funnel Chart**\n\nI\'m now implementing the funnel chart with stacked divs to represent quote retention at each stage. I\'m focusing on accurately reflecting the percentages and counts for each stage, using Tailwind classes for visual representation.\n\n\n**Implementing Top Clients Table**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Top Clientes (Rentabilidad)\" table, focusing on data population and responsive design. I\'m aiming for a clear, organized layout. I\'m focusing on incorporating the client data into the table, and styling the table to match the report\'s design, to ensure a seamless integration. I\'ll need to focus on displaying the data effectively.\n\n\n**Populating Top Clients Table**\n\nI\'m now populating the \"Top Clientes\" table with data and styling it, incorporating the latest design specifications for layout and responsiveness. I\'m focusing on ensuring data alignment. I\'m also now adding the responsive attributes to the client data and their corresponding styles, ensuring correct implementation.\n\n\n**Styling Table Elements**\n\nI\'m now styling the \"Top Clients\" table elements, including numbers and currency. I\'m focusing on ensuring consistent numerical formatting and right alignment for readability. I\'m also now reviewing the table\'s responsiveness, particularly regarding the display and formatting.\n\nI\'m working on ensuring the data is displayed clearly.\n\n\n**Refining Table Alignment**\n\nI\'m now refining the \"Top Clientes\" table, and specifically, I\'m focusing on text and currency alignment within the table cells. I\'m working to ensure the numerical data is right-aligned for readability, and the currency symbols are correctly positioned.\n\n\n**Adding Saved Reports**\n\nI\'m now incorporating the saved reports functionality into the `Reports.tsx` component. I\'m focusing on the component that will feature the saved reports, and the button structure. I\'ve designed the button layout and integrated the list. The spacing and visual cues are being refined.\n\n\n"
